<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n110990" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φῐλήκο-ος</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ον</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀκοή</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>fond of hearing</i> conversation, discourses, etc., 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φ. καὶ ζητητικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Pl.
					<u>R.</u>
					535d
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλόμουσος καὶ φ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				548e
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἵ τε φιλοθεάμονες οἵ τε
			φ.</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				475d
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀνὴρ φ. καὶ ἱστορικός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					<u>Alc.</u>
					10
				</span></i>
			:—<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ φ.,</span>
			
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιληκοΐα</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				2.704e
			</span></i>: but also, <i>fond of hearing</i> for mere pastime, opp.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οἱ φιλομαθοῦντες,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				7.7.8
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">-ως, ἔχειν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hld.
					5.16
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Aristid.
				2.230
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				J.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Chor.
				6.34
			</span></i>
			<i><span class="en">
				p.95
			</span></i> F.-R.</div>
